+## Documents
+
+A task whose input *is* a file returns an object from `hostedPrompt` instead of
+a string:
+
+```ts
+const TASKS = {
+  "extract-pdf": {
+    output: { jsonSchema: /* … */, decode: /* … */ },
+    // The CLI has tools and a filesystem: name the path and let it Read.
+    cliPrompt: (input: Statement) => `Read the statement at ${input.path}`,
+    // A vendor has neither, so the bytes travel.
+    hostedPrompt: (input: Statement) => ({
+      text: "Extract every operation.",
+      document: { data: input.bytes, mediaType: "application/pdf" },
+    }),
+    hostedInstruction: "Return the operations as JSON.",
+    allowedTools: ["Read"],
+  },
+} as const satisfies TaskTable
+```
+
+`data` is a `Uint8Array` — the transport encodes it for the vendor — and
+`mediaType` is the IANA type. The document rides the user turn beside
+`hostedInstruction`, which is the only turn a vendor takes content parts in.
+
+A `hostedPrompt` that returns a plain `string` attaches nothing, and its request
+is unchanged: text-only tasks need no edit and send exactly what they always
+sent. A row has one `Input`, so both columns are written against the whole of it
+even where each reads a different half.
+
+The CLI column has no document form and needs none — it can name a path.
+
